iterations.reply:
I left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and fetching from the metadata service would need filesystem and HTTP authority (`http-client`), neither of which is granted. The WIT world cannot import them, so the body cannot call them. The output is unchanged. If you want those behaviors, the node's `with` clause has to be widened in the graph.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // The host channel stamps the session identity and the delivery result.
        crate::aap::caps::response_channel::send(&reply.text)
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

